# Without this, COPY apps/web apps/web (and COPY apps/api apps/api) drag the HOST's own
# node_modules into the build context - pnpm's node_modules is full of symlinks to absolute
# host paths (e.g. /home/you/project/node_modules/.pnpm/...), which don't exist inside the
# container. Node's module resolution walks up through every node_modules on the way to root,
# so a stale per-workspace node_modules copied in like this SHADOWS the correctly pnpm-installed
# one in the image, breaking resolution in confusing, inconsistent ways depending on what
# happens to be in each dev machine's local install at build time. Found this the hard way -
# see the api/web Dockerfile build-log history if reproducing.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output - regenerated fresh in each build stage, never wanted from the host.
dist
**/dist
**/.tmp

# Everything else that's local-machine-only or irrelevant to the image.
.git
.claude
docs
*.log
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
